# ImageResizer Release Notes

## 2.2.0 (5 Oct 2026)

* Academic presets at the top of the list: presentation slide 16:9 and 4:3,
  thesis / publication figure, conference poster graphic, Moodle / e-learning,
  ID photo 35 × 45 mm. The Full HD preset was merged into "Presentation slide 16:9".
* File size limit (e.g. 2 MB for upload systems): JPEG and WebP lower the
  quality first (not below 40), then the resolution; other formats lower the
  resolution. 1 MB = 1 000 000 bytes, so files also fit limits that use 1024 × 1024.
* GPS location is removed by default even when other EXIF metadata is kept.
  The summary says how many photos had their location removed.
* Fix: decimal values typed with a comma ("0,5") on Polish Windows.

## 2.1.0 (5 Oct 2026)

* Polish language (Polski). The language follows Windows by default and can
  be switched from the header; the window updates immediately and the image
  list is kept. Menus, dialogs and error messages are translated too.
* Polish plural forms and decimal commas (e.g. "3 obrazy · 1,0 MB").
* The preview now scales with the window, so the app fits smaller screens.
* The window opens centered on the screen.
* Settings saved by 2.0.0 are migrated automatically.

## 2.0.0 (5 Oct 2026)

Complete rebuild.

* Batch processing: add many images or whole folders (including subfolders),
  with a progress bar and a Cancel button.
* Drag and drop images or folders from Explorer (Windows).
* Four resize modes: Fit within, Fill and crop, Exact size, Percentage.
* Aspect ratio lock for exact sizes.
* 14 presets: Full HD, 4K, web, email, Instagram, Facebook, YouTube, X, LinkedIn, avatars.
* Output formats: JPEG, PNG, WebP, BMP, GIF, TIFF, or the original format.
* Quality slider for JPEG and WebP.
* Option to keep or strip EXIF metadata. Photos are rotated according to EXIF.
* Configurable file name suffix and output folder. Existing files are never
  overwritten unless you allow it.
* Live preview of the result, including the crop.
* Summary with total size savings and a shortcut to open the output folder.
* Settings are remembered between sessions.
* Keyboard shortcuts: Ctrl+O, Ctrl+Shift+O, Ctrl+R.
* New flat design: teal and orange palette, card layout.

Fixes:

* Resizing used the 500 px preview thumbnail instead of the full-resolution image.
* Crash when saving palette images (GIF) or images with transparency as JPEG.
* Crash on zero or negative sizes and on file names without an extension.
* Temporary preview files were never deleted.
* The application icon was not set in packaged builds.

